  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, there is no evidence to guide exploitation; the priority is to establish a clear, interpretable performance baseline that anchors all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the search space: it uses a deterministic, parameter-free RNA encoder (PCA), a single profile (no aggregation complexity), and no image pipeline. This minimizes confounding factors and running time while giving us the 'floor' performance of the RNA modality. Knowing this baseline is essential before interpreting any multimodal or learned-encoder result: without it, we cannot determine whether a multimodal configuration's accuracy reflects genuine cross-modal synergy or simply the contribution of one modality. It also calibrates how much headroom exists for the other design axes (profile setting, encoder choice, image modality, fusion strategy), making every subsequent experiment more informative under the limited budget."
}

